{"ready":true,"data":{"id":"taika-waititi","name":"Taika Waititi","birthDate":"1975-08-16","birthPlace":"Wellington, New Zealand","bio":"Taika David Cohen ONZM (born 16 August 1975), known professionally as Taika Waititi (/ˈtaɪkə ˈwaɪtiti/ TY-kə WY-tee-tee), is a New Zealand filmmaker, writer, actor, and comedian. He has received numerous accolades including an Academy Award, a BAFTA Award and a Grammy Award, as well as nominations for two Golden Globe Awards and six Emmy Awards. Time magazine named him one of the 100 most influential people in the world in 2022.\n\nHis feature films Boy (2010) and Hunt for the Wilderpeople (2016) have each been the top-grossing film entirely funded and produced within New Zealand. Waititi's 2003 short film Two Cars, One Night earned him an Academy Award nomination for Best Live Action Short Film. He co-wrote, co-directed and starred in the horror comedy film What We Do in the Shadows (2014) with Jemaine Clement, which was adapted into a television series of the same name in 2019. The series has been nominated for the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Comedy Series.\n\nHis directing credits include the superhero films Thor: Ragnarok (2017) and Thor: Love and Thunder (2022), as well as the black comedy film Jojo Rabbit (2019), the last of which he also wrote and starred in as an imaginary version of Adolf Hitler. Jojo Rabbit received six Academy Award nominations and won Best Adapted Screenplay. Waititi also earned a Grammy Award for producing the film's soundtrack.\n\nIn television, Waititi co-created and produced the comedy drama series Reservation Dogs, and directed, produced, and starred in the comedy Our Flag Means Death. In addition to directing an episode of the series The Mandalorian, he voiced the character IG-11, for which he was nominated for the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Character Voice-Over Performance.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Taika Waititi, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.","source":"TMDB","fetchedAt":"2026-11-19T17:44:32+00:00","tmdbId":55934,"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/person/55934","credits":[{"id":"thor-ragnarok","title":"Thor: Ragnarok","character":"Korg (voice)"},{"id":"endgame","title":"Avengers: Endgame","character":"Korg (voice)"},{"id":"thor-love","title":"Thor: Love and Thunder","character":"Korg / Old Kronan God (voice)"},{"id":"whatif-2","title":"What If...? — Season 2","character":"Korg"},{"id":"whatif-3","title":"What If...? — Season 3","character":"Korg"}],"photo":"./public-data/images/people/taika-waititi.webp","filmography":[{"name":"FING!","year":2027,"character":"The Viscount","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/4YB91INfnD8Nu7OPDD7f9T0hd7u.jpg"},{"name":"Charlie vs. the Chocolate Factory","year":2027,"character":"Willy Wonka (voice)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/gHa5V7A23CLntW4PwqKeDu66Smf.jpg"},{"name":"Place to Be","year":2026,"character":"Nelson","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/gdMvMJG8BGIAs9OEuSEnzJbCyn1.jpg"},{"name":"Avatar Aang: The Last Airbender","year":2026,"character":"Gorillavark (voice)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/3sgnSfNT27Bx5O5ukr7B26mhEQq.jpg"},{"name":"Imagine","year":2026,"character":"Zombie Taika (voice)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/gCEzV6zDG9MeeGaYohNWaiw53FK.jpg"},{"name":"LEGO Star Wars: The Mandalorian","year":2026,"character":"IG-11 / IG-12 (voice)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/x3HEvYXWOW6WHqsHmg2MUVy3SLm.jpg"},{"name":"The Great British Bake Off: Second Helpings","year":2026,"character":"Self","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/hyZs4jmChlcytHjZVavndyyxDHN.jpg"},{"name":"Time Bandits","year":2024,"character":"Supreme Being","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ahnTuygdAbjXvLKzLQlK2txosMX.jpg"},{"name":"Conan O'Brien Must Go"